  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><div class="container"><a href="/index.html">Home</a> <span class="sep">/</span> <a href="/tours.html">Tours</a> <span class="sep">/</span> <span>7 Days Silk Road Group Tour</span></div></nav>

<div class="tour-detail-hero" style="background-image: url('/assets/images/hero-silkroad.jpg');">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>7 Days Silk Road Group Tour to Gansu & Qinghai</h1>
    <div class="route">📍 Dunhuang → Jiayuguan → Zhangye → Xining → Chaka</div>
    <div class="badge-row"><span>⭐ 4-Star Hotels</span><span>🎓 English Guide</span></div>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="tour-detail-layout">
  <!-- Main content -->
  <div class="tour-detail-main reveal">
    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>This 7-day Silk Road group tour covers the highlights of Gansu and Qinghai in one unforgettable week. From the ancient Buddhist art of Mogao Caves and the stunning rainbow mountains of Zhangye Danxia to the mirror-like Chaka Salt Lake, experience the best of the Silk Road's eastern section. Travel with a small group, stay in comfortable 4-star hotels, and enjoy the expertise of our English-speaking guides.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Explore the UNESCO-listed Mogao Caves (8 caves)</li><li>Camel ride at the Singing Sand Dunes</li>
      <li>Walk the legendary Jiayuguan Fortress — end of the Great Wall</li><li>Photograph Zhangye Danxia's rainbow mountains at sunset</li>
      <li>Walk on the mirror-like Chaka Salt Lake</li><li>Visit Kumbum Monastery, a sacred Tibetan Buddhist site</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Dunhuang</h4><p>Arrive at Dunhuang Airport. Your guide will meet you and transfer to your hotel. In the evening, explore the bustling Shazhou Night Market — a feast of local snacks, handicrafts, and Silk Road souvenirs.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Dunhuang 4★</span><span>🍽 Dinner</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang — Mogao Caves & Singing Sand Dunes</h4><p>A full UNESCO day. Morning visit to the Mogao Caves (8 caves included), a treasure trove of Buddhist art spanning a thousand years. Afternoon camel ride and sand surfing at the Singing Sand Dunes. Watch the sunset over Crescent Moon Spring, an oasis in the desert.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Dunhuang 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang → Jiayuguan</h4><p>Drive through the Gobi Desert to Jiayuguan (approx. 5 hours). Visit the mighty Jiayuguan Fortress — the western terminus of the Great Wall of China, standing guard at a strategic pass since the Ming Dynasty.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Jiayuguan 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Jiayuguan → Zhangye</h4><p>Morning visit to the Giant Buddha Temple in Zhangye, home to China's largest reclining Buddha (34.5m). Drive to Zhangye (approx. 2.5 hours). Late afternoon at Zhangye Danxia Geopark — the rainbow-colored rock formations are at their most spectacular at sunset.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Zhangye 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Zhangye → Xining (High-speed train)</h4><p>Morning high-speed train to Xining (approx. 3 hours), the gateway to the Tibetan Plateau. Afternoon visit to Dongguan Mosque, one of the largest mosques in northwest China, and stroll through the vibrant Muslim quarter.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Xining 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Xining — Chaka Salt Lake & Kumbum Monastery</h4><p>Full day excursion. Morning drive to Chaka Salt Lake (4 hours), the "Mirror of the Sky." Walk on the salt flats and capture stunning reflection photos. On the return journey, visit Kumbum Monastery (Ta'er Si), one of the six great monasteries of the Gelug school of Tibetan Buddhism.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Xining 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Depart Xining</h4><p>Free time until your airport transfer. Your Gansu & Qinghai adventure concludes. Safe travels and 再见!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🍽 B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What's Included</h2>
    <div class="inc-list">
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>6 nights 4-star hotel accommodation (twin-share)</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>English-speaking guide throughout</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>High-speed train: Zhangye → Xining</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Private air-conditioned vehicle & driver</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Meals as indicated (B=Breakfast, L=Lunch, D=Dinner)</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>All entrance fees & listed activities</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Airport transfers on arrival & departure</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Travel insurance (China domestic)</p></div>
    </div>

    <h2>What's Excluded</h2>
    <div class="inc-list">
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>International flights to/from China</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>Chinese visa fees</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>Personal expenses & tips</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>Single room supplement ($280)</p></div>
    </div>

    </div>

